WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240
Imagine spending suddenly
drops across the whole country.

2
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.200
Factories cut output.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.490
Unemployment climbs
above its natural rate.

4
00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:12.380
Some economists say: no need to act.

5
00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.570
With so many people looking for work,

6
00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:18.290
wages fall, costs fall, and
the economy returns to full

7
00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:20.140
employment on its own.

8
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:22.770
So if a slump ends by itself,

9
00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.790
why would anyone step in?

10
00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.880
In this mission, you'll watch
the recessionary gap close

11
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.010
on the AD and AS graph,

12
00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:31.710
one step at a time.

13
00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.050
Then you'll run the clock in a graph lab

14
00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:38.000
and predict where real GDP
and the price level end up.

15
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.080
Your mission: find out why policymakers
might act instead of waiting.
